/-!
# Genuine analytic regularity in two complex variables

On actual open subsets of `ℂ × ℂ` and `ComplexPlane₂`, continuous functions
with holomorphic one-variable coordinate slices are jointly analytic.
Consequently joint complex differentiability implies `ContDiff ℂ ω`, and
locally uniform limits of holomorphic functions are holomorphic.  The proof
uses two literal one-variable Cauchy formulas and the actual bounded double
circle integral, not an assumed Hartogs or multivariable regularity theorem.
-/
